# One byte sequence per file on every platform.
#
# Several assets here are pinned by SHA-256 and validated against the bytes on
# disk: the bundled scientist personas carry a manifest digest per file, and
# `cli/hatch_build.py` refuses to package a mismatch. A checkout that rewrites
# LF to CRLF therefore does not merely look different, it fails the build — the
# Windows release job died exactly this way, hashing a CRLF `manifest.json`.
# Normalising to LF everywhere keeps a checkout byte-identical to the blob.
#
# `.ps1` is deliberately LF too: the documented installer pipes the raw blob
# into PowerShell (`irm ... | iex`), so LF is already what Windows executes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Digest-pinned: never eligible for conversion, whatever the text heuristics say.
skills/soulagent/assets/builtin-scientist-kg/** -text

# Binary payloads where a silent rewrite would corrupt an index rather than
# announce itself.
*.faiss binary
*.pack binary
*.png binary
